  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Laura_001
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.15
    speaker: Laura
    text: Oh, thank God. That was quick. Is it broken? Can you fix it?
    holdSeconds: 6.0556602
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6c3e007af19b26c4581872b4a3b2ba8f, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Mia_001
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Mia
    text: Let me take a look first.
    holdSeconds: 3.414151
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 88d1c1e7a8241394a82c09dc984d822f, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Laura_002
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Laura
    text: "Please tell me you can fix it tonight. This thing has been a godsend.
      The past year has been\u2014I mean, actually quiet. Ava and I used to blow
      up at each other every other day. She's fourteen."
    holdSeconds: 12
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dfef90ea5bd12a6459f1ff97d05f2410, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Laura_003
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Laura
    text: "Mark and I both work full-time. Nobody's home during the day. It keeps
      Ava company, she tells it things, it fills me in\u2014I actually know what's
      going on with her. And then tonight it just dies out of nowhere?"
    holdSeconds: 12
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a68d01635f37a7e4183547083ab270d4, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Mark_001
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Mark
    text: We tried cycling the power a couple times. Nothing. Screen never came back.
    holdSeconds: 6.0556602
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ae4993a4043b1fe41a7c40b9caafd1f4, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Mia_002
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Mia
    text: Okay. I'll pull the record.
    holdSeconds: 3.0367923
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 04fc26a5fb261e743bc56b527f65d37e, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  - lineId: 17F03_HumanEntryParents_Laura_004
    presentationKind: 0
    dialogueMode: 0
    speakerSide: 0
    advancePolicy: 0
    startDelay: 0.18
    speaker: Laura
    text: Please hurry. Ava has school tomorrow.
    holdSeconds: 3.414151
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6d065d7b1bd272746a6b0660c0895cfe, type: 3}
    durationMode: 0
    voiceTailSeconds: 0.12
  postSequenceDelay: 0.18
